{{Term/Store|Obstacle Course|Obstacle Courses|Series, OoT, OoT3D, BotW|plural}} are a recurring [[Mini-Game]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="Course">{{Cite|Epona looks great! It looks like you were able to tame her too! How about trying your skill with Epona on an {{Color OoT3D|Red|obstacle course}}? I'll time you for {{Color OoT3D|Red|two laps}}. It's pretty challenging. If you miss jumping a fence in the proper order, you'll fail. How about it? Do you want to try?|Malon|OoT3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Guide|BotW Piggyback|page= 332}}</ref>

==Location and Rules==
==={{OoT|-}}===
{{Stub|OoT}}
Once [[Link]] has won [[Epona]] in a race against [[Ingo]] and freed [[Lon Lon Ranch]] from his control, [[Malon]] will begin offering him the chance to participate in her Obstacle Course.<ref name="Course"/> She challenges him to beat her best time of 50 seconds.<ref>{{Cite|The current record is {{Color OoT3D|Red|50 seconds}}. First, try to beat this record! If you can beat this record, I'll give you a present! Give it your best shot, OK? All right, let's get started!|Malon|OoT3D}}</ref>  The Course consists of two laps around Lon Lon Ranch's center pen, using Epona to jump over eight fences of varying heights. Should Link manage to beat Malon's time, he will be rewarded with a [[Cow]] being delivered to his [[Link's House|House]].<ref>{{Cite|You did it! {{Obstacle Course Time}} is the new course record! I have to give you a present to commemorate your new record! The present is a little too heavy to give to you here, so I'll have it delivered to your house. Bet you can't wait to see it! Hee hee!|Malon|OoT3D}}</ref>

Link may repeat the Obstacle Course an unlimited number of times, challenging his own fastest time rather than Malon's, though there is no prize for doing so.

==={{BotW|-}}===
The Obstacle Course is operated by [[Blynne]] at the [[Highland Stable]]. It can be played by speaking to him outside the Stable while riding a tame [[Horse]] and accepting his challenge to see who is the better rider.<ref>{{Cite|I grew up taming horses 'round these parts. I'm confident there's not a rider in Hyrule better'n me.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|And I got just the way to prove it—a li'l game to test which fella's better in the saddle. One I almost never lose.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|What do you think? You got the grit to step up and challenge the master?|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> After [[Link]] pays the 20 [[Rupee]] fee to play, Blynne will set up the obstacles for the [[Mini-Game]] throughout [[Fural Plain]].

Blynne explains that the goal of the Obstacle Course is to navigate all ten [[Obstacle]]s as quick as possible.<ref>{{Cite|It's an obstacle course, but on horseback! There are 10 obstacles to navigate. Best time wins.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> He guarantees that it will teach Link how to ride his Horses better.<ref>{{Cite|If you're not an ace in the saddle when the game starts, I guarantee you'll be one by the time it's through!|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> The difficult part is being able to control one's Horse, instead of riding as fast as possible.<ref>{{Cite|The difficult part about this is the fact that you can't just try to recklessly ride as fast as you can. In order to clear the obstacles on the path, you have to be able to control your horse very well.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> He offers Link [[Horse Gear]] if he can beat his time.<ref>{{Cite|If you can beat my personal best time, I'll give you some mighty fine {{Color BotW|Red|horse gear}}.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref>

Blynne will refuse to start the Mini-Game if the necessary conditions are not met. If Link attempts to speak to him without being atop a Horse, Blynne will tell Link to mount one and come back.<ref>{{Cite|Well shoot, fella. You can't enter a horse race without a horse to ride! Go mount up and come back to me when you're serious.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> Blynne will reject Link if he is riding atop an unregistered Horse, telling Link to handle the paperwork at a Stable first.<ref>{{Cite|That horse you're riding isn't properly {{Color BotW|Red|registered}} yet. Go take care of the paperwork at the stable counter before you come to challenge my best time.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> Additionally, if Link attempts to challenge Blynne while riding atop anything other than a Horse, Blynne will emphasize that the Mini-Game is exclusively meant for Horses.<ref>{{Cite|See here, fella. This is a HORSE race. If you want in, you gotta be on a horse. Not...whatever's happening here.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> If it is [[Rain]]ing, Blynne will not be in the mood to run the Course.<ref>{{Cite|I'm in no mood to run the course when it's raining. If you want to beat my time, come back when the sun's out.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> However, if it starts Raining while Link is attempting the Course, Blynne will still ask if he wants to try again.

Before Link starts the Obstacle Course, Blynne asks if he wants to hear the rules.<ref>{{Cite|You need a rundown of the rules?|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> He explains that Link needs to ride his Horse around Fural Plain while jumping over all of the Obstacles.<ref>{{Cite|Ride your horse around this grassy field while jumping the obstacles.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> Link is not allowed to cross the finish line until he has jumped over all 10.<ref>{{Cite|There are {{Color BotW|Red|10 obstacles}}, all told. You don't get to cross the finish line 'til you've jumped them all. When you clear the last one, ride back here. Simple, right?|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> Additionally, Link will be disqualified if he dismounts his Horse.<ref>{{Cite|Don't dismount your horse, or you're out of the running. Not that you need telling, right?|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> Blynne informs him that his best time is 1 minute and 15 seconds,<ref>{{Cite|My best time's {{Color BotW|Red|1 minute 15 seconds}}. Think you can beat that?|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> though he suggests trying to complete the Course in 1 minute and 30 seconds.<ref>{{Cite|Why don't you aim for {{Color BotW|Red|1 minute and 30 seconds}} first?|Blynne|BotW}}</ref>

Blynne will only reward Link with encouragement if he completes the Obstacle Course with any time over 2 minutes.<ref>{{Cite|Your time was {{Color BotW|Red|02:00.00}}, huh... Keep riding until you've got some hearty saddle sores. Lotta work ahead of you! Your horse may balk when you spur it on right in front of an obstacle. I would too!|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> If Link finishes the Course between 1 minute and 30 seconds and 2 minutes, Blynne will give him a [[Swift Carrot]].<ref>{{Cite|Nice riding, fella! You didn't beat my time, but I'm impressed all the same. Here, this is for your hardworking friend.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link has at least one Swift Carrot in his [[Inventory]], Blynne will instead give him a [[Red Rupee]], valued at 20 Rupees.}} When Link completes the Obstacle Course between 1 minute and 15 seconds and 1 minute and 30 seconds, Blynne rewards him with the [[Extravagant Bridle]].<ref>{{Cite|Here's that {{Color BotW|Red|horse gear}} I promised you. Keep at it, and maybe someday you'll be on my level.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link already owns the Extravagant Bridle but does not have any [[Endura Carrot]]s in his Inventory, Blynne will give an Endura Carrot instead. If Link also has at least one Endura Carrot, he will receive a [[Purple Rupee]], valued at 50 Rupees.}} If Link beats Blynne's time, Blynne will give him the [[Extravagant Saddle]].<ref>{{Cite|Holy smoke, would you look at that? Never thought I'd see the day.. But a man's gotta abide by his word, so here's that {{Color BotW|Red|horse gear}} I promised.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link already owns the Extravagant Saddle, Blynne will give the Extravagant Bridle instead. If Link also has the Extravagant Bridle, he will receive a [[Silver Rupee]], valued at 100 Rupees.}}

